/*
================================================================================
POWER BI DAX MEASURES LIBRARY
Project: E-Commerce Sales & Business Performance Analysis
Author: Senior Data Analyst & Power BI Developer
Target Table: sales_orders (or _AllMeasures table)
================================================================================
*/

// ============================================================================
// 1. CORE VOLUME & REVENUE MEASURES
// ============================================================================

// Measure 1: Total Revenue (Gross Sales)
// Business Explanation: Sum of all net transaction dollar sales invoiced to customers.
Total Revenue = 
SUM(sales_orders[sales])


// Measure 2: Total Cost
// Business Explanation: Total cost of goods sold (COGS) incurred to supply the products.
Total Cost = 
SUM(sales_orders[cost])


// Measure 3: Total Profit
// Business Explanation: Total net earnings generated across all transactions (Sales - Cost).
Total Profit = 
SUM(sales_orders[profit])


// Measure 4: Total Orders
// Business Explanation: Counts distinct purchase transactions / invoices.
// CRITICAL: We use DISTINCTCOUNT(order_id) instead of COUNTROWS because an order 
// can contain multiple line items!
Total Orders = 
DISTINCTCOUNT(sales_orders[order_id])


// Measure 5: Total Units Sold
// Business Explanation: Total count of physical merchandise units shipped.
Total Units Sold = 
SUM(sales_orders[quantity])


// ============================================================================
// 2. FINANCIAL RATIOS & MARGINS
// ============================================================================

// Measure 6: Overall Profit Margin (%)
// Business Explanation: Ratio of net profit to total revenue.
// CRITICAL INTERVIEW RULE: Never average the row-level profit margin column!
// We use DIVIDE() because it handles divide-by-zero safely and returns 0 or blank.
Profit Margin % = 
DIVIDE(
    [Total Profit], 
    [Total Revenue], 
    0
)


// Measure 7: Average Order Value (AOV)
// Business Explanation: Average dollar revenue generated per customer invoice.
Average Order Value = 
DIVIDE(
    [Total Revenue], 
    [Total Orders], 
    0
)


// Measure 8: Average Discount Rate (%)
// Business Explanation: Average promotional discount percentage applied across transactions.
Average Discount % = 
AVERAGE(sales_orders[discount])


// ============================================================================
// 3. TIME INTELLIGENCE & MOM GROWTH
// ============================================================================

// Measure 9: Prior Month Revenue
// Business Explanation: Calculates revenue for the preceding month using the Date Dimension.
Prior Month Revenue = 
CALCULATE(
    [Total Revenue],
    DATEADD('DateTable'[Date], -1, MONTH)
)


// Measure 10: Month-over-Month (MoM) Revenue Growth (%)
// Business Explanation: Percentage rate of sales change from previous month to current month.
MoM Revenue Growth % = 
VAR CurrentRevenue = [Total Revenue]
VAR PreviousRevenue = [Prior Month Revenue]
RETURN
DIVIDE(
    CurrentRevenue - PreviousRevenue,
    PreviousRevenue,
    0
)


// ============================================================================
// 4. DAX CODE FOR DATE TABLE (CALCULATED TABLE)
// Business Explanation: A continuous calendar dimension table required for proper 
// Time Intelligence (MoM, YoY) and relationship modeling.
// ============================================================================
